      "text": "Let $y = x^2$ and solve for $y$ instead. Then the expression is\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{x^4}{x^8 + 2x^6 - 4x^4 + 8x^2 + 16} &= \\frac{y^2}{y^4 + 2y^3 - 4y^2 + 8y + 16} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{y^2 + 2y^{-1} - 4 + \\frac{8}{y^2} + \\frac{16}{y^4}},\n\\end{align*}which becomes\n\\begin{align*}\ny^2 + 2y^{-1} - 4 + \\frac{8}{y^2} + \\frac{16}{y^4} &= \\frac{y^6 + 2y^4 - 4y^4 - 8y^2 + 16y^2 + 64}{y^4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{y^6 - 6y^4 + 8y^2 + 64}{y^4} \\\\\n&= y^2 \\left( y^4 - 6y^2 + 8 + \\frac{64}{y^2} \\right) \\\\\n&= y^2 \\left( y^4 + \\frac{64}{y^2} + 8y^2 - 8y^2 + 8 \\right) \\\\\n&= y^2 \\left( \\left( y^2 + \\frac{8}{y^2} \\right)^2 + 16 \\right) \\\\\n&\\ge 16,\n\\end{align*}with equality when $y^2 + \\frac{8}{y^2} = 8 \\Rightarrow y = \\sqrt{3}.$ Thus, the required maximum is $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{16}}.$\nThe answer is: \\frac{1}{16}",
