      "text": "The maximum value is $\\boxed{1/8}$...\nLet $x^2 = t$.\nThen, the expression becomes $\\frac{t^2}{t^4+2t^3-4t^2+8t+16}$.\nSince the costant 16 is positive, we can find the value of $x$ for $x^4+2x^3-4x^2+8x+16=0$, which $x=1$. Furthermore, the maximum value is $\\frac{t^2}{t^4+2t^3-4t^2+8t}= \\frac{x^4}{x^8+2x^6-4x^4+8x^2+16} \\leq\\frac{x^4}{(x-1)^2+2x^2-4x+27}   = \\boxed{1/8}$.",
